<file path="README.md">
# Infina AI — Landing (React + HTML Reference)

**Infina AI** marketing landing surfaces. Dual-surface model: a canonical React landing bundle (source of truth) and six standalone HTML pages (upstream marketing reference). This repo is the engineering source.

## The React Landing Harness

The React bundle (`src/`) is the canonical engineering deliverable. It's a **Vite 5** + **React 18** + **TypeScript 5** verification harness that compiles the landing components in isolation. The bundle flows one-way into `infina-pfa-80389` (the production PFA app that builds/deploys landing). See **[landing-source-of-truth.md](docs/landing-source-of-truth.md)** for the sync contract and drift guards.

**Quick start:**
```bash
npm install
npm run dev              # Start Vite dev server (http://localhost:5173)
npm run build           # Compile React bundle
npm run typecheck       # Type-check TypeScript
npm run preview         # Preview production build
```

Stack: React 18.3.1 + react-router-dom 6.30.1 + react-helmet-async 3.0.0 + Vite 5.4.19 + TypeScript 5.8.3.

## The Six HTML Pages (Upstream Marketing Reference)

Upstream marketing reference pages (no build, no framework). Used for creative direction and content evolution. Marketing edits HTML → dev hand-ports to React → syncs to PFA. The HTML site remains unretired and can still be hosted statically (legacy deploy instructions still apply).

| File | Route Intent | Purpose |
|------|--------------|---------|
| `home.html` | `/` | Umbrella story — three product lines (Work / Inside / Personal) |
| `work.html` | `/work` | Infina AI Work — specialist agents for company functions |
| `inside.html` | `/inside` | Infina AI Inside — embeddable AI specialists for partners |
| `personal.html` | `/personal` | Infina AI Personal — consumer AI specialists for everyday decisions |
| `focus-alignment.html` | `/work/focus-alignment` | Deep-dive on Focus & Alignment agent |
| `about.html` | `/about` | Company story, timeline, differentiators |

Each page uses two Web Component scripts for shared nav/footer:
- `nav.js` — `<infina-nav>` top bar with active highlight + mobile hamburger.
- `footer.js` — `<infina-footer>` bottom strip with logo, links, copyright.

To run the HTML site locally:
```bash
python3 -m http.server 8080
# open http://localhost:8080/home.html
```

Or serve via `npx serve .` or open `home.html` directly in a browser.

## Assets

- `assets/` — lifestyle imagery (travel photos) for Personal page cards.
- `uploads/` — brand logos (BIDV, MBB, VCB, Prudential, AIA, Bao Viet, PVI, MWG, HPG, VIC, Petrolimex, Kafi, Zalopay, etc.) + lifestyle photography + master Infina logo.
- `src/styles/landing.css` — canonical token set (colors, typography, spacing) also lives in the React bundle.

## Project Docs

- `docs/landing-source-of-truth.md` — Sync contract between this repo and PFA (the drift guard).
- `docs/project-overview-pdr.md` — Product Development Requirements for both the React bundle and HTML reference.
- `docs/codebase-summary.md` — React bundle structure + HTML module summary.
- `docs/code-standards.md` — React/TS conventions + HTML/CSS/JS rules.
- `docs/system-architecture.md` — React harness topology + asset pipeline + HTML topology.
- `docs/design-guidelines.md` — Brand tokens, typography, layout patterns (unified across both surfaces).
- `docs/deployment-guide.md` — Deploy React bundle to PFA + legacy HTML static hosting.
- `docs/project-roadmap.md` — Current phase: React port iteration + PFA sync. Phase 5 (SSG migration) superseded.

## Repository Layout

```
.
├── package.json                  # React bundle metadata + scripts
├── vite.config.ts               # Vite configuration
├── tsconfig.json                # TypeScript project references
├── index.html                   # Vite harness entry (13 lines)
├── src/
│   ├── main.tsx                 # React harness entry (providers, router)
│   ├── App.tsx                  # Route table (6 pages mapped to /,/work,/inside,/personal,/about,/focus-alignment)
│   ├── pages/landing/           # 6 page components + LandingLayout
│   ├── components/landing-v2/   # React landing components
│   │   ├── layout/              # LandingNav, LandingFooter (React versions)
│   │   ├── sections/            # LeadSection (lead form)
│   │   └── pages/               # per-page section components
│   └── styles/                  # landing.css (base), landing-*.css (per-page)
├── public/landing-html/uploads/ # asset mirror (via setup-harness-assets.mjs)
├── scripts/
│   ├── setup-harness-assets.mjs # copy uploads/ → public/ before dev/build
│   └── sync-landing-to-pfa.sh   # one-way sync to PFA + drift manifest
├── dist/                        # build output (gitignored)
├── home.html                    # HTML pages (upstream reference)
├── work.html
├── inside.html
├── personal.html
├── focus-alignment.html
├── about.html
├── nav.js                       # Web Component for HTML nav
├── footer.js                    # Web Component for HTML footer
├── assets/                      # lifestyle imagery
├── uploads/                     # brand logos + photography
├── docs/                        # project documentation
└── plans/                       # implementation plans & reports
```

## Brand & Tech Snapshot

- **Brand color:** `#001F5C` (deep navy) with `#1863DC` highlight. Tokens live in `src/styles/landing.css` `:root` (React) and HTML page `<style>` blocks.
- **Typography:** Be Vietnam Pro (Google Fonts), 400/500/600/700.
- **React harness:** Vite dev/build, React Router, Helmet for meta. Compiles in isolation for verification before PFA sync.
- **HTML site:** Plain HTML + inline styles + vanilla Custom Elements. No build step, no framework.
- **No analytics/tracking** yet; static pages only.
- **Import alias:** `@/` resolves to `src/` (mirrors PFA's setup for identical import paths).

## Conventions

- Page-level styles live inline in each HTML file's `<head><style>` block.
- Shared chrome (nav, footer) styles live inside the corresponding JS Custom Element.
- File and asset names use kebab-case.
- Commit messages follow conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, etc.) — no AI references.

See `docs/code-standards.md` for the full set of rules.
</file>

